WEBVTT

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.540
Would you like some wine?

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.110
Uh, w-well...

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.380
Do you have oolong tea?

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.510
Yes, I'll go prepare some.

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:29.400
I'll have apple cider!

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.490
I'll have a Bireley's soda!

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:33.050
How about you?

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:36.070
I'll... I'll have a Bireley's soda, too.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:38.060
Another Bireley's, please!

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:41.720
Cheers!

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.420
Look at Naoko-san. Our blushing bride's quite the drinker!

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.330
Akagawa-senpai's gonna have his hands full.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.700
His face is already beet red!

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:59.370
<i>Although I'm ashamed to admit it,
my only desire at this moment</i>

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:02.150
<i>was to plunge into the alluring world of adulthood all by myself.</i>

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:07.460
<i>In other words, I wished to be freed of the chains of etiquette and
the presence of my seniors and drink as much as I possibly could!</i>

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.190
You still haven't gotten tired of staring at her?

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.540
I... I was just looking that way by chance, all right?

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.480
<i>I was completely head over heels for her.</i>

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:39.670
<i>She had grabbed hold of my heart at first sight when she joined my club as my junior last year,</i>

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:43.760
<i>and ever since that day, I'd committed myself to the SEE Strategy!</i>

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:49.140
Senpai, what a coincidence!

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:51.470
I was just passing through by chance!

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:54.040
Such a coincidence!

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:55.010
By chance!

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:56.750
Coincidence...

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:57.430
Chance!

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:57.920
Coinc...

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:58.260
Chance!
Coinc...

00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:58.620
Co...

00:01:58.620 --> 00:01:59.260
Chance!
Co...

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:02.470
<i>My goal was to appear in front of her as frequently as possible,</i>

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:06.460
<i>and thus, the SEE Strategy entails being Seen Everytime Everywhere.</i>

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:09.350
<i>This ensures our meetings push beyond the realm of mere chance,</i>

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:12.780
<i>and she'll have no choice but to feel the red string of fate!</i>

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.560
<i>My chance is ripening!</i>

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.500
<i>What I need now is the courage to wait!</i>

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.570
That's not exactly courage.

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:20.460
Stop reading my mind!

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:23.300
You sure do love waiting outside the castle for the perfect time to invade.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:27.130
Are you gonna plant an apple tree while you're out there? Maybe build a cottage?

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:30.130
<i>The School Festival Executive Director, and also, my friend.</i>

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:32.330
<i>The most photographed person on campus,</i>

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:35.490
<i>he receives the most Valentine's chocolate in all of Sakyo-ku.</i>

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:38.060
<i>He also maliciously puts his beauty to use through cross-dressing,</i>

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:42.140
<i>and his infamy rose after confusing several young men during the Fall Festival.</i>

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:43.580
You dithering fool!

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:46.230
She's right in front of your face, yet you do nothing!

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:49.070
Hey now, you're drinking too much.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:50.770
<i>Meet my other friend,</i>

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:55.080
<i>who six months ago vowed to never change his underwear until his wish came true.</i>

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.590
<i>Despite smashing the previous record for doing so,</i>

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:01.050
<i>and earning the glorious title of "Don Underwear,"</i>

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.910
<i>his wish, naturally, is as yet unfulfilled.</i>

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:03.970
Leave it alone already!

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:06.330
I'll strike when my iron is hot!

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:08.530
Your iron, huh...

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.250
<i>Tonight's my chance!</i>

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:15.300
<i>If I can take a strategic position at her table when we go to the after-party,</i>

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.460
<i>I can march to the next stage for sure!</i>

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.850
Not romantic!

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:30.420
Now then, we'll be heading off to the next pub!

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:33.230
Anyone who is taking part, please follow me!

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:36.360
It will be a three minute walk,
so take care not to get separated!

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.640
You're all coming, right?

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:38.860
Right?!

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.830
<i>In the neighborhood of Shijo-Kiyamachi,</i>

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:56.200
<i>men and women indulging in evening pleasures flowed in an incessant stream.</i>

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.390
<i>Surely </i>this <i>place would have what I sought:</i>

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:00.650
<i>an encounter with glorious alcohol!</i>

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:03.010
<i>The dazzling world of adulthood awaits!</i>

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.340
One piña colada, please!

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:49.080
<i>I like to partake in cocktails.</i>

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:52.820
<i>Picking a cocktail is like picking out a sparkling jewel—</i>

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:55.520
<i>everything about it feels so luxurious.</i>

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:12.540
<i>In all honesty, my love for rum is so pure that the entire Pacific Ocean could be made of it for all I care.</i>

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:15.870
<i>I long to down the entire bottle the second I lay hands on one,</i>

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:18.800
<i>but that's the sort of dream you're better off locking away in your heart.</i>

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.800
Looks like you can hold your drink, sweetheart.

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:24.030
Have one on me.

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:25.360
Oh no, I couldn't!

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.580
Get this gal an Acapulco!

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:30.720
Rum's made from sugarcane, you know.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:35.040
Brandy was originally known as <i>vin brule</i>, or "burnt wine."

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:38.080
Once you distill wine, the alcohol content skyrockets,

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:40.440
and that's how you end up with brandy and whisky.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.170
You certainly know a lot.

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:43.880
Just part of gettin' old.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:45.950
I'm sorry I won't be able to keep up.

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:49.720
Don't you worry. Spending time with people I pass by in the night...

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:51.200
That's where I find my joy.

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:57.620
Have you heard of a legendary drink out there called Fake Denki Brandy?

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:58.710
"Fake"?

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:02.910
Denki Brandy was cooked up by a well-known joint in Asakusa back in the 1800s.

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:04.870
A truly classic cocktail.

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:08.700
These days it's big enough that you'll find the stuff in convenience stores,

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:12.290
but the recipe was kept under lock and key for ages.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:14.320
However, one day,

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:16.770
some guy working for Kyoto Central Telephone

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:19.980
got the bright idea to try replicating its flavor.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:22.700
After traveling down blind alleys of trial and error,

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:24.960
what he discovered at the end of his journey

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:27.490
was what's now known as Fake Denki Brandy.

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:33.730
Its taste, its scent...

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:36.110
They're totally different from Denki Brandy,

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:39.170
but the mysterious and enticing flavor it <i>does</i> have...

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:41.730
It's still being made in secret somewhere

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:44.260
and being smuggled through the streets as we speak.

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:47.010
I'd really like to give it a try...

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:49.510
You're a girl after my own heart!

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.130
Hey, you!

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:54.020
You on the hunt for some good girls tonight?

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:57.120
No thank you!

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.600
I'm searching for a raven-haired maiden!

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:00.450
So, black hair is what you're after...

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:01.570
That's not what I meant!

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:03.280
Don't take this personally.

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:10.890
Looking at you brings back memories of my daughter.

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:13.230
I was never the greatest father to her...

00:07:13.230 --> 00:07:15.140
Been a while since we met face to face.

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:17.300
Not like I got the right to see her anyway...

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:19.700
This is one of the most important days of her life...

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:21.700
And I stood her up...

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:25.930
Young lady!

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:29.440
Never forget to grab onto happiness with your own hands!

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:31.820
Find out what's valuable and hold tight!

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:32.890
Yessir!

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:34.450
Go and give it your all!

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:35.180
Yessir!

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:37.860
Give it your all...

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:38.810
Yessir!

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.800
G-Give it your all...

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:43.910
Toudou-san.

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:45.190
Give it your all—

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:52.200
You sure showed him, girl!

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:57.210
Oh? Well, this is rather shameless.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:59.290
Th-This is erotic art!

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:01.170
I'm an art collector, damn it!

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:03.810
Toudou's well-known for being a gross old pervert.

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:06.180
He's just a piece of shit from top to bottom.

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:08.630
A grope here or there ain't gonna hurt nothin'!

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:14.950
You mustn't let your guard down against people you meet while out on the town at night.

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:17.180
Us two are no exception, of course.

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:23.870
He's part of some gross group called the Bedchamber Investigation Team.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:26.080
All he does is collect that perverted stuff!

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:28.460
I hear his business isn't going so well these days

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:31.780
and that he's found himself deep in debt as a result.

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:35.400
Well, it's not for a tengu like me to know how the vulgar masses live their lives.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:40.500
I guess I did something awful.
I wouldn't have punched him if I'd known...

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:41.680
It's fine, it's fine!

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:43.820
Be as awful and cold-hearted as you like!

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:46.140
But y'know, you sure have one hell of a punch.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:48.280
That's what I call my Friendship Punch.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:50.720
My mother taught it to me when I was little.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:52.090
Do you understand?

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:56.220
As you make your way through this world,
you will learn that the noble number but a few.

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:58.240
What's left are utter fools and rotten fiends,

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:00.750
or quite possibly utterly foolish rotten fiends.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:04.120
Such encounters demand the use of the Friendship Punch.

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:07.150
When you wrap your thumb in your four fingers like so,

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:10.150
your fist becomes as lovable as the paw of the Lucky Cat.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:13.010
Such a fist can no longer truly convey feelings of hatred.

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:15.800
Thus, we are freed from the cycle of violence,

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:18.770
and thus we invite harmony into this world.

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:21.570
This is my trump card,

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:26.750
the only technique my parents taught me that I'm permitted to use in the outside world.

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:29.880
You certainly seem wise beyond your years!

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:32.020
Perhaps you'd like to join us tonight?

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:34.410
We'll show you how things are done in Ponto-cho!

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:35.620
I would love that!

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:37.050
But I don't have much more money...

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:38.350
No need to worry.

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:41.050
It's been several years since I've had money either.

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:43.270
Put it on Toudou's tab, okay?

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:46.270
Money is indeed quite nomadic.

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:50.780
If you mark some, it's not unheard of to come across it again in your life.

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:53.780
Looks like Rihaku-san is up to his old tricks...

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:56.310
Have you heard of that crazy old loan shark?

00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:59.240
The one who goes around in that luxurious three-story tall train!

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.960
He's a big collector of old books, antiques,

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:05.300
and apparently, the underwear stolen off young men!

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:08.440
Ew, Higuchi! Wearing used pants like that is totally gross!

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:12.580
He also has quite the collection of a drink called Fake Denki Brandy.

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:13.800
The one from the legend?

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:17.190
This worked out pretty well, actually.

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:19.970
Higuchi-kun doesn't wear any underwear!

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:27.300
Excuse me, would anyone...

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:30.420
Would anyone happen to have some pants?

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:31.580
Damn it...

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:33.110
Why's this gotta happen to me...

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:34.360
Hey, young'n!

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:36.090
You lookin' for some help?

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:36.830
Yes!

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:38.780
Some pants, please!

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:41.550
Then get up here and help me drown my sorrows!

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:43.370
We're gonna get plastered!

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:56.600
Now take a good look and see how she does things.

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:00.930
Yay!

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:02.430
Who are you?!

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:04.630
Who cares! You out for a drink?

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:05.390
Yay!

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:06.550
I-I am...
Yay!

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:07.930
Then let's get plastered!

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:10.890
Let's go down all of the booze in Kiyamachi!

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:12.220
Yay!

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:13.510
Yay!

00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:14.500
Let's go!
Yay!

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:16.860
We've breached the walls, and we mustn't hesitate.

00:11:17.490 --> 00:11:19.400
Shame will only give you away here.

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:24.330
Waltzing in uninvited is a test of one's will—
will you sink, or will you swim?

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:27.230
So you just want to be a spectator, my dear?

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:29.630
Not the ears!

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:31.780
If you don't have talent, then work hard!

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:34.840
Working hard <i>requires</i> talent!

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:35.560
And therefore...

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:37.590
Talent is born from hard work!

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:40.230
What kind of gathering is this?

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:42.330
A grand assembly of quibbles and semantics.

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:43.630
That's not it at all!

00:11:43.630 --> 00:11:44.850
It's called sophistry!

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:46.100
Oh, and you...

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:50.610
Which is better, marrying the man you love or the one you don't?

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:55.230
The man you <i>don't</i> love is a far better choice!

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:58.700
Once love enters the picture,
one loses all sense of reason,

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:02.150
but choosing a man you don't love allows you to make rational judgments!

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:04.000
This is a lifelong decision, after all,

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:08.120
so it needs to be a rational choice born strictly of prudence!

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:09.750
These so-called feelings of love

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.960
can't be explained with any rationality!

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:15.310
They shouldn't be part of marriage in the first place!

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:19.040
Feelings of love will never cool for one you never felt love for in the first place!

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:22.420
Infidelity won't burden you with jealousy!

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:27.550
Rationality practically demands that women should marry men they don't love...

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:28.990
So why <i>do</i> they marry for love?

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:30.560
We're at this guy's farewell party!
So why <i>do</i> they marry for love?

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:31.680
Why can't they see the truth?!
We're at this guy's farewell party!

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:33.820
He got jilted and he's off to study in London!
Why can't they see the truth?!

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:35.570
Damn it!

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:37.610
Who the hell wants to go to England?!

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:40.440
Naoko-san!

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:40.990
Now then!

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:44.620
Let us celebrate the future prospects of Kousaka-senpai in London!

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:46.490
Begin the Sophism Samba!

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:49.610
Go off and become a great man!

00:12:49.610 --> 00:12:53.150
Make something of yourself—and never come back!

00:12:53.150 --> 00:12:55.420
Don't worry, we'll be fine without you!

00:12:58.920 --> 00:12:59.910
Thank you!

00:12:59.910 --> 00:13:03.430
It's an immense joy being sent off by gentlemen like you!

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:05.730
Shall we head off to Ponto-cho now?

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:12.690
Well, hello!

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:14.550
My, but it's been a while!

00:13:14.550 --> 00:13:16.280
This is a 60th birthday celebration.

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:18.570
That's wonderful! You wanna drink?

00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:20.260
My son's wedding was today.

00:13:20.260 --> 00:13:22.070
All the more reason to drink!

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:23.930
Boy, life sure goes by fast...

00:13:23.930 --> 00:13:25.300
What is "life," anyway?

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:27.380
Life is living.

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:29.060
So when your life ends you die?

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:31.660
No no no, death is just what we call the end of life.

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.910
So then life and living are different?

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:37.210
Well, this is a drag.

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:40.000
No one's touching any of the Akadama Punch I brought...

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:42.330
Higuchi-kun, are you a tengu or not?

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:44.110
Come on, liven up this party!

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:46.510
Well, I'm not sure if I can lift spirits this low,

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:49.100
but I'll try my Higuchi-Style Flying Technique.

00:13:56.610 --> 00:13:57.720
Boring...

00:13:57.720 --> 00:13:59.030
Why's he wearing pants?

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:02.690
My spectators

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:04.110
are worse off than I thought.

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:07.530
I wish it were more lively in here...

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:09.560
Us old folks are running out of time!

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:11.530
The hours are only getting faster...

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:14.120
Young lady, you mind if I see your watch?

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:15.140
Oh, my!

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:16.080
It's so slow!

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:17.130
Isn't this normal?

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:18.880
This is what ours look like.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.650
And look how that compares to ours!

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.890
Time certainly does fly...

00:14:29.140 --> 00:14:30.930
You're keeping a good pace!

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:31.780
Huh?!

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:35.940
You polished all of these off, did you?

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:37.980
You sure can hold your stuff!

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:40.210
I drink until there's nothing left!

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:42.640
She's the real deal.

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:48.460
I may be plain, unpolished, and less interesting than a rice cooker.

00:14:48.460 --> 00:14:51.100
But here and now, I demand you all point and laugh!

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:57.700
C'mon, what the heck are you doing?

00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:59.950
That's... That's the Sophist Samba!

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:02.760
The Sophist Samba we thought up so long ago!

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:05.020
Okay, everyone, join in!

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:09.100
This is from those carefree days we spent dabbling in sophistry!

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:10.650
This takes me back!

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:12.230
We were exactly like eels!

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:14.800
Slippery and slimy, no one could pin us down!

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:19.270
It appears that she's this evening's leading lady.

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:22.270
I'm touched to think that our tradition would live on today!

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:24.780
The cherished desire of any alum of the Sophistry Club!

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:28.880
Well, let's keep this Dance of Burdens to the Next Generation going!

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:31.330
Now, drink up!

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:34.150
A talent like yours only comes along once a century!

00:15:34.150 --> 00:15:36.520
You should challenge Rihaku to a drinking contest!

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:38.350
Against <i>him</i>? I suppose she could!

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:41.620
If you win against him, he'll grant any wish you desire!

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:44.520
You could drink Fake Denki Brandy to your heart's content.

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:46.800
That's a challenge I'm happy to meet!

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:48.710
I'd bet on you to win for sure!

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:49.580
Me too!

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:51.180
And me as well!

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:56.470
C'mon, ain't you gonna drink with me?!

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:58.270
Chug! Chug!

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:00.980
Uh, I don't think you're supposed to force people to chug...

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:02.440
Who gives a shit?!

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:05.270
I'll make ya if I <i>wanna</i> make ya!

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:08.910
Back in the '80s bubble, I was rollin' in dough...

00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:11.450
Now, that's just a far-off dream.

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:13.490
The final blow was that tornado the other day.

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:18.810
Whirling down from Fushimi Castle,
it came roaring towards my koi carp nursery!

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:23.790
All of my beloved koi were sucked up,
sent swirling into the night sky!

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:25.080
Yuko!

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:26.270
Jirokichi!

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:28.800
Dagnabbit!

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:30.350
Gimme back Yuko!

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:32.900
Gimme back Jirokichi!

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:34.400
Um, excuse me...

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:36.690
Could I get those pants now?

00:16:36.690 --> 00:16:40.510
You think a scum-sucking student like you <i>deserves</i> pants?!

00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:44.760
I got to where I was by bustin' my ass through my own naked merits...

00:16:44.760 --> 00:16:46.540
Damn it!

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:50.470
Toudou-san!

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:53.840
Is it true you're going to let go of your collection?

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:55.850
Go away!

00:16:55.850 --> 00:16:58.460
I got it rough, y'know?!

00:16:58.460 --> 00:16:59.710
May I have a look?

00:17:01.710 --> 00:17:04.710
And these are such splendid ones, too...

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:06.620
Hey, young man!

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.090
You're lookin' like you wanna call me a creep!

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:10.090
I didn't say anything!

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:12.650
We're the Bedchamber Investigation Team.

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:16.650
We only seek to gather artifacts of our sensual cultural heritage.

00:17:16.650 --> 00:17:19.340
"What ya really mean is you collect porn!"

00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:21.020
That's what you wanna say, right?!

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:22.850
Again, I didn't say anything!

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:25.110
That asshole's comin' after my collection...

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:28.490
He offered me that sweet loan, which tore my daughter away from me...

00:17:28.490 --> 00:17:31.820
And now he's tearin' away my erotic art, the only friend I got left!

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:35.470
When will Rihaku-san get here?

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:38.330
He's gonna be coming to a restaurant on the Kamo river any minute now...

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:39.050
All right!

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:41.010
I'll go contact everyone in Bedchamber!

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:44.130
We'll all send these ladies off with one final viewing.

00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:45.900
Thank you!

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:48.100
Thank you...

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:49.630
You're comin' too!

00:17:56.350 --> 00:17:57.910
Over here!

00:17:57.910 --> 00:17:58.890
Okay!

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:07.190
Rihaku, come out and play...

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:09.110
Rihaku, come out and play!

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:22.500
Rihaku, come out and play!

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:29.590
Rihaku, come out 'n' play!

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:34.550
No, you're doing it all wrong!

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:36.070
Leave <i>all</i> your shame behind!

00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:36.970
Yo!

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:40.110
Rihaku, come out and play!

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:41.230
What's this?!

00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:42.780
Would you look at that!

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:44.030
It just sort of happened.

00:18:44.030 --> 00:18:45.470
Naoko-san!

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:46.780
Yasuo!

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:56.710
Such a tragic loss!

00:18:56.710 --> 00:18:59.490
This is a hard reset on cultural anthropology!

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:03.890
"Why are grown men cryin' their asses off over erotic art?!"

00:19:03.890 --> 00:19:05.900
That's the kinda look you got in your eyes!

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:09.200
For the last time, I don't care!
You're the one who cares!

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:14.010
It sounds like some hero is challenging Rihaku-san to a drink-off.

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:15.660
Some kind of madman, more like!

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:19.760
I hear he's runnin' around Kiyamachi tearin' the place apart.

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:22.430
I heard he's six meters tall.

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:25.060
A giant wearing a ragged old yukata!

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:26.910
I hear he can shoot koi out of his mouth!

00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:30.820
He came here all the way from far-off Oshu!

00:19:30.820 --> 00:19:32.820
Less a hero, more a monster.

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:33.820
A sleeping giant!

00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:34.820
A fallen monk!

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:41.900
Who on earth are <i>you</i> people?!

00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:45.140
Just those who wield sophistry to become slippery as eels!

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:46.410
My love is happy.

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:48.730
And knowing that, I am happy too!

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:49.820
Banzai!

00:19:49.820 --> 00:19:50.880
Banzai...

00:19:54.470 --> 00:19:56.010
What's going on up there?

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:58.810
Augh, I'm ruined!

00:19:58.810 --> 00:20:00.700
Toudou-san, don't give in to despair!

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:01.730
It doesn't matter!

00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:04.270
I'll just let that ol' bastard kill me,
it'll serve you people right!

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:05.380
How picturesque.

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:06.550
Dad?

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:07.520
Naoko?

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:10.070
I'm gonna die of shame here! Goddamnit!

00:20:10.070 --> 00:20:11.180
Knock it off already, Dad!
I'm gonna die of shame here! Goddamnit!

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:13.520
I don't care if you're a big perv!
I'm gonna die of shame here! Goddamnit!

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:15.140
Naoko-san!

00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:16.050
Kousaka-kun?

00:20:16.050 --> 00:20:16.970
I'm begging you!

00:20:16.970 --> 00:20:18.660
Please, marry me instead!

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:20.350
If you truly love that man,

00:20:20.350 --> 00:20:22.620
I'm begging you to not marry him!

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:24.520
Yes, we've been over this...

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:26.040
No idea what your point is, though.

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:28.200
Kousaka, you're an embarrassment to men!

00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:30.040
Why are you still in Japan?

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:37.090
At last, he takes the stage.

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:52.620
<i>Toudou-san. How good to see you again.</i>

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:54.020
<i>Where are the goods?</i>

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:57.110
That punk kid ruined them!

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:58.660
Man, that's gross...

00:20:58.660 --> 00:20:59.610
Don't say that.

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:02.820
<i>So you haven't kept your word.</i>

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:06.120
<i>How do you plan on settling your debts now?</i>

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:07.770
He's gonna kill me!

00:21:07.770 --> 00:21:09.120
<i>Bring him to me.</i>

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:12.470
Wait right there!

00:21:15.130 --> 00:21:16.630
Huh? It's you!

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:19.480
Toudou-san! You mustn't give up.

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:21.590
There's always another next step in life!

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:23.490
But why would you...

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:27.990
I'm the guy who threw around erotic art and felt you up!

00:21:27.990 --> 00:21:31.640
True, but you still introduced me to a wonderful way to view life.

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:33.170
Rihaku-san!

00:21:33.170 --> 00:21:34.930
I shall be your opponent tonight.

00:21:34.930 --> 00:21:37.690
I challenge you to a drinking contest!

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:39.650
And I will most certainly be the victor.

00:21:39.970 --> 00:21:41.650
Quite the development.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:47.160
<i>As you wish.</i>

00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:07.220
That's my—

00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:10.110
This floor is the bathhouse.

00:22:10.110 --> 00:22:12.480
We'll find the banquet hall below.

00:22:30.450 --> 00:22:32.900
Fake Denki Brandy.

00:22:32.900 --> 00:22:36.500
Alcohol as transparent as pure water.

00:22:36.990 --> 00:22:40.420
If I prove victorious, his debt is doubled.

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:42.420
You'll have no mercy from me.

00:22:49.220 --> 00:22:53.070
If you so allow me, I shall act as judge.

00:22:53.070 --> 00:22:55.730
Now then, begin!

00:23:11.240 --> 00:23:14.980
The taste of Fake Denki Brandy is life's futility.

00:23:20.840 --> 00:23:24.810
To me, the taste is like having my life filled from top to bottom with warmth.

00:23:24.810 --> 00:23:26.260
Luxurious and abundant.

00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:32.880
You're a brat who knows nothing of life.

00:23:32.880 --> 00:23:34.500
Life is empty.

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:38.120
Plentiful.

00:23:45.440 --> 00:23:46.880
Truly empty.

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:52.490
Life is isolation and hollowness,

00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:54.750
gone in an instant.

00:23:55.660 --> 00:23:57.750
<i>Life is nothing but taking.</i>

00:23:57.750 --> 00:23:58.750
<i>Giving.</i>

00:23:58.750 --> 00:23:59.750
<i>Anguish.</i>

00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:00.750
<i>Joy.</i>

00:24:03.510 --> 00:24:05.260
So why are you out tonight?

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:08.160
I'm merely following my thread of fate.

00:24:09.360 --> 00:24:12.330
I believe everything, even drinking with you,

00:24:12.330 --> 00:24:15.730
is connected somehow.

00:24:15.730 --> 00:24:17.460
That's only the deception of the drink.

00:24:17.460 --> 00:24:19.580
You'll understand soon enough.

00:24:19.580 --> 00:24:23.490
Reality is a bleak world full of nothing but lust and greed.

00:24:23.490 --> 00:24:25.640
There are no connections between people.

00:24:25.640 --> 00:24:27.040
Only isolation...

00:24:32.440 --> 00:24:34.330
I...

00:24:35.300 --> 00:24:38.240
Can't go on...

00:24:40.310 --> 00:24:42.620
Victory goes to the young lady!

00:24:45.750 --> 00:24:47.290
Thank you!

00:24:47.290 --> 00:24:48.800
Thank you so much!

00:24:48.800 --> 00:24:52.460
My gosh, is your stomach bottomless?

00:24:52.460 --> 00:24:54.870
Yahoo!

00:25:00.230 --> 00:25:01.390
Don't mind me.

00:25:31.150 --> 00:25:32.010
What?!

00:25:38.130 --> 00:25:39.220
<i>Upon first glance,</i>

00:25:39.220 --> 00:25:42.580
<i>the only people sitting alongside the Kamo River were couples.</i>

00:25:43.260 --> 00:25:46.840
<i>They're so evenly spaced.
Is there some sort of rule about that?</i>

00:25:51.030 --> 00:25:52.590
So chilly...

00:25:52.590 --> 00:25:56.030
Don't talk nonsense. You don't find it humid?

00:25:56.530 --> 00:25:58.050
Thanks.

00:26:00.040 --> 00:26:01.030
What do we have here?

00:26:01.030 --> 00:26:03.540
A flyer for the Evening Used Book Market.

00:26:03.540 --> 00:26:05.180
They're already starting that?

00:26:10.300 --> 00:26:13.780
<i>Suddenly, I was being pulled through time by all the books I'd read,</i>

00:26:13.780 --> 00:26:16.760
<i>and I was drawn back to my old picture book, Ra Ta Ta Tam.</i>

00:26:17.030 --> 00:26:23.100
<i>It's a story about a small white train that escapes the house
it's been trapped in and goes on strange adventures.</i>

00:26:23.690 --> 00:26:27.230
<i>How did I ever manage to lose a book as wonderful as that one?</i>

00:26:28.250 --> 00:26:31.810
<i>I set out to lay eyes on it once again!</i>

00:26:38.600 --> 00:26:39.710
You're awake?

00:26:41.040 --> 00:26:43.250
This is the School Festival Committee Office.

00:26:43.250 --> 00:26:45.380
It used to be HQ for the Library Police,

00:26:45.380 --> 00:26:49.790
an organization formed to collect overdue library books from students.

00:26:50.390 --> 00:26:53.270
Furnished with the latest in surveillance equipment,

00:26:53.270 --> 00:26:56.640
every scrap of information on our students is gathered here.

00:26:57.710 --> 00:27:00.810
The work of the School Festival Committee is taxing indeed.

00:27:00.810 --> 00:27:05.140
To ensure our merry fools of students make a soft landing with harsh reality,

00:27:05.140 --> 00:27:08.540
we keep a firm grip on every detail of their desires and actions,

00:27:08.540 --> 00:27:10.510
anticipating every one of their next moves.

00:27:11.150 --> 00:27:13.080
So why I am here?

00:27:15.530 --> 00:27:17.160
No way.

00:27:17.160 --> 00:27:19.030
D-Don't tell me...

00:27:19.030 --> 00:27:19.990
That's right.

00:27:20.490 --> 00:27:24.040
Naturally, we've collected info on <i>her</i> as well.

00:27:28.540 --> 00:27:29.340
This...

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:31.500
This is...

00:27:31.910 --> 00:27:33.760
This is illegal, isn't it?!

00:27:34.780 --> 00:27:36.860
So you don't want to know?

00:27:47.060 --> 00:27:48.750
I suppose you'd call this an exchange,

00:27:48.750 --> 00:27:53.130
but I was hoping you would help me as a friend regardless.

00:27:53.130 --> 00:27:55.230
There are just so many troublemakers,

00:27:55.230 --> 00:27:57.810
and I worry about our ability to keep a lid on things.

00:27:57.810 --> 00:28:00.440
The girl is a fan of a book named Ra Ta Ta Tam.

00:28:00.440 --> 00:28:02.030
Ever since reading it as a girl,

00:28:02.030 --> 00:28:03.990
the book has acted as her guiding light,

00:28:03.990 --> 00:28:06.540
and it appears that she's suddenly remembered it.

00:28:10.540 --> 00:28:13.050
Where can I get my hands on that book?

00:28:13.370 --> 00:28:15.700
There are many options for both old and new copies,

00:28:15.700 --> 00:28:20.260
from online auctions to bookstores of several shapes and sizes.

00:28:20.260 --> 00:28:22.440
However, the exact copy she had as a child

00:28:22.440 --> 00:28:25.860
has just reappeared on the market as a used book.

00:28:25.860 --> 00:28:27.480
Th-Then...

00:28:27.480 --> 00:28:28.310
Take a look.

00:28:28.310 --> 00:28:31.610
It's expected to appear at the Shimogamo Evening Used Book Market.

00:28:32.210 --> 00:28:35.610
If you were to obtain this, how easy it would be to claim her heart!

00:28:42.490 --> 00:28:44.560
<i>A veritable sea of books!</i>

00:28:44.560 --> 00:28:46.330
<i>I was a fish in the deepest depths,</i>

00:28:46.330 --> 00:28:48.580
<i>gliding this way and that in search of prey!</i>

00:29:05.970 --> 00:29:08.730
Viva beginner's luck!

00:29:10.730 --> 00:29:13.900
<i>Why is it still so damn hot this time of night?</i>

00:29:13.900 --> 00:29:16.200
<i>I can't stand used books.</i>

00:29:16.200 --> 00:29:19.910
<i>Books call out in deceit,
"Read us and get a little wiser,"</i>

00:29:19.910 --> 00:29:23.190
<i>but never once have I put any of that wisdom to practical use.</i>

00:29:23.190 --> 00:29:25.950
<i>O books, grant me not wisdom, but grace and charm!</i>

00:29:25.950 --> 00:29:28.120
<i>But after that, feel free to grant me wisdom as—</i>

00:29:32.750 --> 00:29:35.340
Whaddya think you're doing?! You better pay up!

00:29:35.340 --> 00:29:37.300
That's my line, buster!

00:29:37.300 --> 00:29:39.930
You don't see you're the one who needs to apologize?

00:29:39.930 --> 00:29:42.470
Hmph, you've got your mind on a girl, huh?

00:29:42.470 --> 00:29:43.320
What?!

00:29:43.320 --> 00:29:45.630
"If I get my hands on her beloved book,

00:29:45.630 --> 00:29:47.550
it'll be a cinch to claim her heart."

00:29:47.550 --> 00:29:49.730
That's what you're thinking, right?

00:29:49.730 --> 00:29:51.230
Th-That's too on the nose!

00:29:55.480 --> 00:29:58.550
<i>If one suddenly finds the book they've spent years searching for,</i>

00:29:58.550 --> 00:30:03.670
<i>or when one remembers a book from their past and it appears out of nowhere in front of them,</i>

00:30:03.670 --> 00:30:06.770
<i>the pull of the thread of fate can be felt, clear as day.</i>

00:30:07.790 --> 00:30:10.500
<i>Almost like there is a God of the Used Book Market.</i>

00:30:10.500 --> 00:30:14.470
<i>A god who can fashion a happy encounter with the book I desire,</i>

00:30:14.470 --> 00:30:18.420
<i>who can bring me back to forgotten books from my past...</i>

00:30:18.420 --> 00:30:20.210
<i>At least, that was my gut feeling.</i>

00:30:21.620 --> 00:30:24.500
<i>But Ra Ta Ta Tam was nowhere to be found.</i>

00:30:24.500 --> 00:30:28.230
<i>I suppose even the God of the Used Book Market doesn't work this late at night.</i>

00:30:28.230 --> 00:30:29.720
I'm feelin' the same as you...

00:30:29.720 --> 00:30:31.810
The books I really want are nowhere to be found.

00:30:31.810 --> 00:30:35.730
Some nasty collector's got a tight grip on the rare stuff.

00:30:36.090 --> 00:30:37.170
You heard me?

00:30:37.170 --> 00:30:40.730
Y'know, way back when, books traveled from person to person!

00:30:40.730 --> 00:30:42.630
A book is reborn each time it's passed on.

00:30:42.630 --> 00:30:44.460
It's one of the things that ties us together.

00:30:44.460 --> 00:30:48.620
But it's like that damn collector's put up a dam to stop the flow of books.

00:30:49.240 --> 00:30:52.290
Holdin' shadowy auctions for all his rare books,

00:30:52.290 --> 00:30:55.240
where only fools who don't value their lives take part.

00:30:55.240 --> 00:30:56.820
Quite the terrible thing...

00:30:56.820 --> 00:30:58.960
Aah! Wait! You stupid brat!

00:30:58.960 --> 00:31:00.780
You yanked off the price tags! Stop!

00:31:00.780 --> 00:31:02.690
Stop, I said, stop!

00:31:02.690 --> 00:31:04.780
Stop, c'mon, stop, I said!

00:31:07.530 --> 00:31:09.460
Damn that stupid kid.

00:31:09.460 --> 00:31:12.310
I can't believe he made me buy him a new ice cream cone...

00:31:12.310 --> 00:31:14.970
But at least that's all over with now.

00:31:15.770 --> 00:31:17.920
Hey kid, give it up already!

00:31:17.920 --> 00:31:19.440
Huh? The heck?

00:31:19.440 --> 00:31:21.400
What the hell is this?!

00:31:23.790 --> 00:31:26.820
This guy's the one who made me do it!

00:31:26.820 --> 00:31:30.470
If I didn't, he said he was gonna molest me!

00:31:30.470 --> 00:31:31.570
So I...

00:31:32.330 --> 00:31:33.080
Hey you.

00:31:33.080 --> 00:31:35.440
Why don't you come with me.

00:31:35.440 --> 00:31:37.060
H-Hold on! Wait!

00:31:37.060 --> 00:31:38.170
I didn't do...

00:31:38.170 --> 00:31:40.840
What is he doing with that kid?

00:31:42.220 --> 00:31:44.010
He was going to molest that child...

00:31:44.010 --> 00:31:45.620
Hope you like prison, kid.

00:31:45.620 --> 00:31:46.890
I'm sure I won't!

00:31:46.890 --> 00:31:47.580
Hey!

00:31:47.580 --> 00:31:48.670
Where'd that brat go?!

00:31:48.670 --> 00:31:50.510
What's goin' on here, kid?

00:31:50.510 --> 00:31:53.520
More trousers trouble, huh?

00:31:58.210 --> 00:31:59.190
Hey!

00:32:02.360 --> 00:32:03.780
You out for a drink?

00:32:06.350 --> 00:32:09.090
An ice kotatsu? How refined!

00:32:09.090 --> 00:32:12.110
Higuchi-san, are you going to read all of these books?

00:32:12.110 --> 00:32:13.200
Heaven forbid!

00:32:13.490 --> 00:32:16.960
I'm selling these to an acquaintance of mine at quite a markup.

00:32:17.540 --> 00:32:19.620
I must express my gratitude for books.

00:32:19.620 --> 00:32:24.960
To think people would pay so handsomely for nothing more than paper stained with ink.

00:32:24.960 --> 00:32:28.390
Anyone who collects dirty things like those is a total moron!

00:32:32.050 --> 00:32:34.710
I had quite the harvest today.

00:32:34.710 --> 00:32:37.830
If you're interested, I'll treat you to some yakisoba as well.

00:32:37.830 --> 00:32:39.150
Thank you very much!

00:32:39.150 --> 00:32:40.880
Higuchi-kun treating someone?

00:32:40.880 --> 00:32:43.100
That happens about once every quarter century!

00:32:46.890 --> 00:32:49.260
My, it appears even more profit is on the table.

00:32:49.260 --> 00:32:52.570
I have another matter to attend to,
so please wait here for my return.

00:32:52.570 --> 00:32:55.210
Oh! This guy here's Don Underwear.

00:32:55.210 --> 00:32:58.180
He's quite the hardcore romanticist!

00:32:58.180 --> 00:32:59.790
I am no romanticist.

00:32:59.790 --> 00:33:04.320
I'm simply a man toiling to once again meet his fated love.

00:33:04.320 --> 00:33:05.050
See what I mean?

00:33:05.590 --> 00:33:08.050
It sounds like there's a story there!

00:33:09.110 --> 00:33:11.290
It was during last year's School Festival...

00:33:11.290 --> 00:33:14.300
After watching a friend's nonsensical play,

00:33:14.300 --> 00:33:16.600
I took a seat on a bench.

00:33:19.230 --> 00:33:21.780
Suddenly, a rain of apples began to fall.

00:33:21.780 --> 00:33:22.860
Apples?

00:33:22.860 --> 00:33:26.440
Most likely, some students were transporting them to make candy apples,

00:33:26.440 --> 00:33:29.400
and they spilled simultaneously on the floors above.

00:33:30.300 --> 00:33:32.240
And so, down below, at the same time,

00:33:32.240 --> 00:33:34.290
apples bounced off both our heads.

00:33:41.580 --> 00:33:44.680
At that moment, it was like my heart was shot from my chest!

00:33:45.100 --> 00:33:46.950
There was no doubt it was love!

00:33:46.950 --> 00:33:49.120
Surely, this was the work of fate.

00:33:51.370 --> 00:33:54.970
However, I had no idea what to do next.

00:33:55.350 --> 00:33:58.440
Our entire relationship was having apples bounce off our heads,

00:33:58.440 --> 00:34:00.760
and so I hesitated to ask her name.

00:34:02.550 --> 00:34:04.060
And ever since she left...

00:34:05.480 --> 00:34:08.370
Not a day has gone by where I haven't thought of her.

00:34:10.060 --> 00:34:12.060
I simply wanted to see her again and speak to her!

00:34:12.060 --> 00:34:14.110
I would not give in to hesitation!

00:34:14.810 --> 00:34:17.770
However, I hadn't the faintest idea how to search for her

00:34:17.770 --> 00:34:20.620
and could not bring myself to depend
on sinister spy organizations.

00:34:20.620 --> 00:34:22.880
Everything was chance arranged by fate.

00:34:22.880 --> 00:34:25.130
The entire incident had the flair of the romantic!

00:34:25.130 --> 00:34:27.460
More like Don Romantic, huh?

00:34:27.460 --> 00:34:31.190
And thus, I went to Yoshida Shrine and I made my vow.

00:34:31.190 --> 00:34:33.330
Until the day I laid eyes on her again...

00:34:33.330 --> 00:34:36.140
Until then, I would never remove the pair of underwear I wore!

00:34:36.140 --> 00:34:37.090
Oh, my!

00:34:37.090 --> 00:34:39.890
I think you've got some wires crossed in that head of yours...

00:34:47.290 --> 00:34:48.840
Thank you so much!

00:34:48.840 --> 00:34:50.820
No need for all that.

00:34:50.820 --> 00:34:52.760
People know me.

00:34:52.760 --> 00:34:53.830
Well then, I'll...

00:34:53.830 --> 00:34:56.650
The ol' koi nursery's starting to rally again,

00:34:56.650 --> 00:34:59.100
so I'm rebuilding my erotic art collection.

00:34:59.100 --> 00:35:00.470
How nice for you!

00:35:00.470 --> 00:35:01.580
Well, I'll see you—

00:35:02.540 --> 00:35:04.890
There's a shadowy auction goin' on tonight,

00:35:04.890 --> 00:35:08.460
and a lost piece by Katsushika Hokusai himself is on the list.

00:35:08.460 --> 00:35:09.530
But wouldn't y'know,

00:35:09.530 --> 00:35:12.800
they're holdin' it somewhere I'm not exactly welcome.

00:35:12.800 --> 00:35:14.190
Ah, well, you see...

00:35:14.190 --> 00:35:15.700
I saved you, didn't I?

00:35:15.700 --> 00:35:17.800
Does "give-and-take" mean anything to you?

00:35:27.800 --> 00:35:29.810
Higuchi's there, too...

00:35:29.810 --> 00:35:31.600
I'll wait here! Go on ahead!

00:35:31.600 --> 00:35:32.530
I'm beggin' ya!

00:35:32.530 --> 00:35:34.870
I'll reward ya handsomely!

00:35:34.870 --> 00:35:36.700
I'm countin' on ya! Good luck!

00:35:37.520 --> 00:35:39.880
So... What the heck is going on here?

00:35:39.880 --> 00:35:44.240
This is a feast for demons. Take care you don't end up on the menu.

00:35:44.240 --> 00:35:45.960
Contestants, if I may have your attention...

00:35:45.960 --> 00:35:47.590
Please come this way.

00:35:55.790 --> 00:35:57.690
This is how Rihaku-san likes it.

00:35:57.690 --> 00:35:59.590
What's with this overbearing air?

00:36:12.610 --> 00:36:14.830
A humble welcome to my jamboree!

00:36:14.830 --> 00:36:17.360
Now this is what you call a hot pot, eh?

00:36:17.360 --> 00:36:20.130
If you add some sesame oil, you'll find it very tasty.

00:36:24.500 --> 00:36:25.430
My eyes!

00:36:26.620 --> 00:36:29.700
To whoever lasts the longest at my table,

00:36:29.700 --> 00:36:34.330
I shall grant the right to take from my shelf whichever book they please.

00:36:34.330 --> 00:36:36.630
I trust all of you have a prize in mind.

00:36:37.010 --> 00:36:37.760
The manuscript
of the Kokinshu!

00:36:37.760 --> 00:36:38.760
The diary of
Kishida Ryusei
is my white whale.

00:36:38.760 --> 00:36:39.760
The Steam Train/
Steamship Trip
Guide 1st Edition!

00:36:39.760 --> 00:36:41.260
The erotic art

00:36:41.260 --> 00:36:46.230
This is a picture book that once belonged to a certain raven-haired child.

00:36:46.230 --> 00:36:48.520
Have a look—her name's written right there.

00:36:53.270 --> 00:36:55.620
<i>My Romantic Engine went full throttle!</i>

00:36:55.620 --> 00:36:56.860
<i>Ra Ta Ta Tam lay before me.</i>

00:36:56.860 --> 00:36:59.030
<i>Not only that, the copy she had as a child!</i>

00:36:59.030 --> 00:37:01.980
<i>Surely that makes it the most valuable thing under the heavens!</i>

00:37:02.530 --> 00:37:03.950
Now then, your first course.

00:37:03.950 --> 00:37:06.540
How about you all begin with one piece each.

00:37:22.800 --> 00:37:25.050
Spicy!

00:37:42.230 --> 00:37:43.310
Hold on, young man!

00:37:43.310 --> 00:37:44.570
You mustn't be naughty!

00:37:44.830 --> 00:37:46.070
I'm not being naughty!

00:37:46.070 --> 00:37:47.920
I'm doing something good here!

00:37:47.920 --> 00:37:49.260
Something good?

00:37:49.260 --> 00:37:50.580
Onee-chan, did you know?

00:37:51.030 --> 00:37:53.580
Every book is connected.

00:37:54.770 --> 00:37:58.080
For example, that girl has the entire Sherlock Holmes collection.

00:37:58.080 --> 00:37:59.590
Take the author, Conan Doyle.

00:37:59.590 --> 00:38:02.670
Getting inspiration from the French author Jules Verne,

00:38:02.670 --> 00:38:05.390
he wrote the science-fiction novel "The Lost World."

00:38:05.390 --> 00:38:07.430
That's that book over there.

00:38:07.430 --> 00:38:12.210
Now, Verne was inspired by Alexandre Dumas to write Mathias Sandorf.

00:38:12.210 --> 00:38:16.500
Dumas' work, "The Count of Monte Cristo,"
came to Japan under the name "The Cavern King."

00:38:16.500 --> 00:38:19.710
The first to adapt it was Kuroiwa Ruiko of the Yorozu Morning News.

00:38:19.710 --> 00:38:23.220
And he in turn appeared as a character in the novel "The Meiji Tower of Babel."

00:38:23.220 --> 00:38:25.290
The author of that was Yamada Futaro.

00:38:25.290 --> 00:38:27.090
In his "War Generation Anti-War Diaries,"

00:38:27.090 --> 00:38:29.860
Yamada declared the novel
"Oni Fire" to be utter rubbish.

00:38:29.860 --> 00:38:31.400
That was written by Yokomizo Seishi.

00:38:31.400 --> 00:38:34.050
He was an editor at the magazine "Shin Seinen" in his youth,

00:38:34.050 --> 00:38:37.450
and his co-editor at the time was Watanabe On, author of "The Androgynous Scion."

00:38:37.450 --> 00:38:41.540
Tanazaki Jun'ichiro submitted an article titled "Harusamu" to honor him after his death.

00:38:41.540 --> 00:38:44.970
Tanazaki himself engaged in fierce literary dispute with Akutagawa Ryunosuke.

00:38:44.970 --> 00:38:47.450
Months after the dispute,
Akutagawa took his own life.

00:38:47.450 --> 00:38:50.990
Uchida Hyakken explored the particulars of this suicide in "Bowler Hat."

00:38:50.990 --> 00:38:53.490
This work was then praised by Mishima Yukio.

00:38:53.490 --> 00:38:57.770
At the age of 22, Mishima declared his hatred of Dazai Osamu directly to Dazai's face.

00:38:57.770 --> 00:39:01.410
Dazai wrote an article in memory of a friend who died of tuberculosis—

00:39:01.410 --> 00:39:03.600
the author of that book there, Oda Sakunosuke.

00:39:03.600 --> 00:39:07.950
All books are connected. This sea of used books is in truth one giant book!

00:39:07.950 --> 00:39:10.450
What on earth are you?

00:39:11.150 --> 00:39:13.870
I'm the God of the Used Book Market!

00:39:14.300 --> 00:39:18.770
I loose my divine wrath on those who stop the flow of books by locking them away.

00:39:18.770 --> 00:39:21.630
My duty is to return those books
to the sea they came from!

00:39:22.490 --> 00:39:25.380
And I'd like you to help me!

00:39:38.190 --> 00:39:40.190
You're certainly packing it away!

00:39:40.190 --> 00:39:43.320
If you tire of the hot pot,
we also have ramen and gyoza!

00:39:56.400 --> 00:40:00.110
Don't you think it's about time you gave up?

00:40:00.110 --> 00:40:02.200
Right back at you.

00:40:03.280 --> 00:40:07.620
Just make sure to quit once you start hallucinating rainbow streamers.

00:40:07.620 --> 00:40:11.300
Are you sure you're not seeing them yourself?

00:40:11.760 --> 00:40:13.110
<i>I had already forgotten pain.</i>

00:40:13.110 --> 00:40:14.930
<i>My consciousness had grown dim.</i>

00:40:14.930 --> 00:40:19.060
<i>Intent only on defeating the hot pot in front of me, I was now a perpetual motion machine.</i>

00:40:19.060 --> 00:40:21.500
You're persistent, aren't you...

00:40:21.500 --> 00:40:25.680
You've made me push myself further than I ever have before.

00:40:26.160 --> 00:40:29.100
I'm starting to hallucinate things like this.

00:40:31.430 --> 00:40:33.700
That's got nothing on my illusions!

00:40:58.330 --> 00:41:00.190
Bravo!

00:41:00.190 --> 00:41:02.280
You are the victor, young man!

00:41:02.280 --> 00:41:03.440
Take your book and go!

00:41:13.320 --> 00:41:15.330
Thank you sho, sho mush...

00:41:19.170 --> 00:41:20.580
H-Huh?!

00:41:21.290 --> 00:41:22.680
What's this?

00:41:24.370 --> 00:41:26.590
It is I, the God of the Used Book Market!

00:41:26.590 --> 00:41:28.710
It's that kid!

00:41:28.710 --> 00:41:31.930
Impudent collector, reap what you have sown!

00:41:42.520 --> 00:41:44.460
The Steam Train/Steamboat Trip Guide!

00:41:44.460 --> 00:41:47.790
The manuscript for the Kokinshu!

00:41:48.400 --> 00:41:51.530
If you want them, go scour the sea of used books!

00:41:51.530 --> 00:41:55.760
I believe you'll find them in appropriate places at appropriate prices.

00:41:57.540 --> 00:41:59.560
Damn it all to hell!

00:41:59.560 --> 00:42:01.670
My collection!

00:42:09.300 --> 00:42:12.300
Stop! My destiny is waiting!

00:42:13.840 --> 00:42:15.300
Isn't that...

00:42:15.980 --> 00:42:18.310
the Senpai I keep bumping into?

00:42:19.850 --> 00:42:21.620
Onee-chan! Thanks a lot!

00:42:21.620 --> 00:42:23.640
Those books have been resurrected.

00:42:23.640 --> 00:42:27.690
I bet you'll come across
Ra Ta Ta Tam any minute now!

00:42:33.700 --> 00:42:35.870
Th-This is the diary of Kishida Ryusei!

00:42:35.870 --> 00:42:36.880
Why is it here?!

00:42:36.880 --> 00:42:39.130
Oh, I'm so grateful!

00:42:39.130 --> 00:42:39.800
The manuscript of the Kokinshu!

00:42:39.800 --> 00:42:41.520
The Steam Train/Steamboat Trip Guide!
The manuscript of the Kokinshu!

00:42:41.520 --> 00:42:42.460
The Steam Train/Steamboat Trip Guide!

00:42:43.370 --> 00:42:44.710
How unfortunate...

00:42:44.710 --> 00:42:47.380
Betrayed by the God of the Used Book Market.

00:42:47.380 --> 00:42:48.960
How utterly annoying.

00:42:48.960 --> 00:42:51.220
Why don't I treat you to yakisoba instead?

00:42:52.310 --> 00:42:54.560
Hanuki-san, maybe you'd better go home.

00:42:54.560 --> 00:42:56.970
This way!

00:42:56.970 --> 00:43:00.040
Hey ho!

00:43:04.370 --> 00:43:05.140
What's this?

00:43:05.140 --> 00:43:06.580
Guerrilla theater.

00:43:06.580 --> 00:43:09.180
It's time for the School Festival already?

00:43:09.180 --> 00:43:11.360
The Crackpot of Monte Cristo! Scene 47!

00:43:13.200 --> 00:43:16.790
You there! Are you Jogasaki,
the head of the Film Club Misogi?

00:43:16.790 --> 00:43:18.610
How dare you address me without "-san"!

00:43:18.610 --> 00:43:20.650
Tell me your name this instant!

00:43:20.650 --> 00:43:22.560
I am Princess Daruma!

00:43:22.560 --> 00:43:25.700
I'm searching for the Crackpot of Monte Cristo, now tell me where he is!

00:43:25.700 --> 00:43:27.950
No! Kaori!

00:43:27.950 --> 00:43:30.880
That's lower than low, you trollop!

00:43:34.630 --> 00:43:37.690
If I were to cover this thing in curry

00:43:37.690 --> 00:43:40.530
And leave it for the Mt. Yoshida stray dogs

00:43:40.530 --> 00:43:42.530
Oh, how much fun that would be!

00:43:42.530 --> 00:43:46.480
Stop this now! Don't you dare treat Kaori as a mere object!

00:43:46.480 --> 00:43:48.740
I truly do not know

00:43:48.740 --> 00:43:52.110
Where to find the Crackpot of Monte Cristo

00:43:52.110 --> 00:43:55.520
And that is the honest truth

00:43:55.520 --> 00:43:56.900
However...

00:43:56.900 --> 00:43:58.490
However?

00:43:58.490 --> 00:44:00.180
If you don't spit it out...

00:44:00.180 --> 00:44:01.450
Stop, please!
If you don't spit it out...

00:44:01.450 --> 00:44:04.860
Oh, my beloved Crackpot of Monte Cristo

00:44:04.860 --> 00:44:07.220
Where can I find him now?

00:44:07.220 --> 00:44:10.560
The School Festival Executive Director knows...

00:44:10.560 --> 00:44:12.650
The Festival Director knows?

00:44:12.650 --> 00:44:14.970
Your compatriot in Breast Rock Climbing

00:44:14.970 --> 00:44:17.510
Your friend from the Bedchamber Investigation Team?

00:44:17.510 --> 00:44:20.020
Yes, the one who gave me handholds shaped like breasts

00:44:20.020 --> 00:44:22.410
My friend and rival in Breast Rock Climbing!

00:44:22.410 --> 00:44:24.460
My junior in the Bedchamber Investigation Team

00:44:24.460 --> 00:44:27.290
The School Festival Executive Director knows!

00:44:27.510 --> 00:44:27.690
Kaori!

00:44:27.690 --> 00:44:28.520
You, with your obsessive clean freak tendencies
Kaori!

00:44:28.520 --> 00:44:30.560
You, with your obsessive clean freak tendencies

00:44:30.560 --> 00:44:33.460
You who will never accept intimacy with real flesh and blood

00:44:33.460 --> 00:44:36.340
Acknowledge the filthiness of your own soul

00:44:36.340 --> 00:44:37.780
And apply some bleach

00:44:38.340 --> 00:44:41.610
Finally, I know the villain

00:44:41.610 --> 00:44:44.500
The mastermind is revealed

00:44:44.500 --> 00:44:49.460
My enemy is none other than the
School Festival Executive Director!

00:44:49.460 --> 00:44:51.430
Kaori!

00:44:53.360 --> 00:44:54.270
Take it down, guys!

00:44:54.270 --> 00:44:55.000
Hey ho!

00:44:55.000 --> 00:44:56.450
Stop right there!

00:44:56.450 --> 00:44:58.930
Guerrilla theater is a violation of the rules!

00:44:58.930 --> 00:45:00.020
Hey ho!

00:45:00.020 --> 00:45:02.150
You public-moral-flouting scoundrels!

00:45:02.150 --> 00:45:03.490
After them!

00:45:06.310 --> 00:45:10.000
It appears that your presence extends the night somewhat.

00:45:10.000 --> 00:45:12.820
You can be on your way. I'll watch over Hanuki.

00:45:12.820 --> 00:45:14.490
We'll meet at the School Festival.

00:45:14.490 --> 00:45:15.070
Okay!

00:45:15.070 --> 00:45:17.450
And I recommend buying some Ajari mochi on your way.

00:45:17.450 --> 00:45:19.620
When it's fresh, it's to die for.

00:45:25.740 --> 00:45:28.750
<i>And so, I made my way towards the School Festival.</i>

00:45:29.860 --> 00:45:31.750
<i>This night was far from over!</i>

00:45:34.630 --> 00:45:37.740
<i>A school festival is where cheap youthful energy is shoved in your face.</i>

00:45:37.740 --> 00:45:39.680
<i>You could call it a black market of youth!</i>

00:45:41.210 --> 00:45:42.070
A picture book?

00:45:42.070 --> 00:45:43.840
There's just one?

00:45:43.840 --> 00:45:44.570
Hey, now!

00:45:44.570 --> 00:45:46.480
We're not taking new customers.

00:45:47.180 --> 00:45:49.040
<i>There were no more obstacles in my path!</i>

00:45:49.040 --> 00:45:51.670
<i>I'd obtained a key item needed to invade the castle.</i>

00:45:51.670 --> 00:45:54.690
<i>All I needed to do now was wait for the raven-haired maiden to appear!</i>

00:45:54.690 --> 00:45:56.040
This is Ra Ta Ta Tam!

00:45:56.040 --> 00:45:57.510
Such a coincidence!

00:45:57.930 --> 00:46:00.700
This is no coincidence! It was meant to be!

00:46:00.700 --> 00:46:02.120
<i>And thus we'd finally talk...</i>

00:46:02.120 --> 00:46:04.200
<i>About love, about our futures!</i>

00:46:04.200 --> 00:46:06.900
<i>My long battle is on the verge of drawing to a close!</i>

00:46:06.900 --> 00:46:10.500
<i>Already I smile and grow nostalgic upon reflection of this journey...</i>

00:46:10.500 --> 00:46:11.060
Over there!

00:46:11.060 --> 00:46:11.710
Hey ho!
Over there!

00:46:11.710 --> 00:46:13.680
Hey, stop it! Don't you "hey ho" me!

00:46:13.680 --> 00:46:16.460
What are you doing?! That was my stall, damn it!

00:46:16.460 --> 00:46:17.500
Wait!

00:46:17.500 --> 00:46:19.130
The Crackpot of Monte Cristo!

00:46:19.130 --> 00:46:20.530
Hey!

00:46:22.220 --> 00:46:23.980
Those damn Crackpots...

00:46:23.980 --> 00:46:25.510
What the heck was that about?

00:46:25.510 --> 00:46:27.560
You! We'll convene at headquarters!

00:46:27.560 --> 00:46:31.240
They're a School Festival terrorist group intent on guerrilla theater.

00:46:31.240 --> 00:46:35.430
They steal the frameworks of unpopular festival stalls and use them to build stages.

00:46:35.430 --> 00:46:36.960
Their play is "The Crackpot of Monte Cristo."

00:46:36.960 --> 00:46:41.770
It's an adventure musical about Princess Daruma's
search for the eponymous Crackpot.

00:46:41.770 --> 00:46:45.910
Plot twists involving actual students and clubs are woven
into the story, making for a mix of truth and fiction,

00:46:45.910 --> 00:46:49.940
and those who've had their dirty secrets revealed have fallen hard from grace.

00:46:49.940 --> 00:46:53.530
Allowing their gallivanting to continue any longer would be a mark on our pride.

00:46:53.530 --> 00:46:55.570
The Crackpot of Monte Cristo must be stopped!

00:46:55.570 --> 00:46:57.830
We must return order to the School Festival!

00:46:57.830 --> 00:46:58.770
Yes, sir!

00:47:02.590 --> 00:47:03.600
Director!

00:47:05.110 --> 00:47:07.980
Director, what should we do about the Speedy Kotatsu?

00:47:07.980 --> 00:47:09.890
That's lower on the priority list.

00:47:11.670 --> 00:47:14.690
But sir, they're treating passersby to helpings of hot pot!

00:47:14.690 --> 00:47:17.350
Food poisoning is a risk if we leave them unchecked.

00:47:17.790 --> 00:47:18.960
Take care of it.

00:47:20.610 --> 00:47:22.370
You've got a lot to deal with.

00:47:22.370 --> 00:47:25.880
You're not wrong. Everyone everywhere
is running roughshod!

00:47:27.360 --> 00:47:28.410
Got a cold?

00:47:28.410 --> 00:47:31.440
I picked it up at another of my functions.

00:47:35.370 --> 00:47:37.310
Congratulations!

00:47:37.880 --> 00:47:40.710
Your prize is this red carp backpack!

00:47:41.520 --> 00:47:44.440
Just put your arms through here to wear it!

00:47:44.440 --> 00:47:45.090
Perfect!

00:47:45.560 --> 00:47:46.680
Cool, ain't it?

00:47:46.680 --> 00:47:48.500
<i>My back was now nice and warm!</i>

00:47:48.500 --> 00:47:51.890
<i>I won this red carp just as I was getting chilly!</i>

00:47:51.890 --> 00:47:53.380
<i>Three cheers for opportunism!</i>

00:47:53.380 --> 00:47:54.390
<i>Hail and amen!</i>

00:47:56.160 --> 00:47:58.190
<i>Truly, this was a theater chock full of youth.</i>

00:47:58.190 --> 00:48:01.690
<i>There were so many splendid works by talented students on display.</i>

00:48:01.690 --> 00:48:04.550
<i>Each flowed by like illustrations from some fantastic picture book.</i>

00:48:04.550 --> 00:48:05.190
All right!
<i>Each flowed by like illustrations from some fantastic picture book.</i>

00:48:05.190 --> 00:48:06.700
No way.

00:48:10.700 --> 00:48:11.710
You sure can drink!

00:48:11.710 --> 00:48:12.700
I'm not done yet!

00:48:12.700 --> 00:48:14.910
Well, what about wafers? Those are like bread!

00:48:14.910 --> 00:48:17.960
If you believe that nonsense,
then rice crackers are a type of rice!

00:48:18.470 --> 00:48:20.960
My, that's a splendid red carp you have.

00:48:21.240 --> 00:48:22.150
Higuchi-san!

00:48:22.150 --> 00:48:23.960
It's a warm kotatsu this time, huh?

00:48:23.960 --> 00:48:26.100
Would you care for some hot pot?

00:48:26.100 --> 00:48:28.470
We're on the run from the School Festival Committee.

00:48:28.470 --> 00:48:30.720
The stakes sure have risen...

00:48:30.720 --> 00:48:32.130
Please put your mind at ease.

00:48:32.130 --> 00:48:33.690
While my underwear remains on,

00:48:33.690 --> 00:48:35.370
I shall not go under the kotatsu.

00:48:35.370 --> 00:48:36.230
How admirable.

00:48:36.230 --> 00:48:39.260
Such is the etiquette required of Don Underwear.

00:48:39.260 --> 00:48:42.730
He's about to undertake the greatest battle of his life.

00:48:42.730 --> 00:48:43.950
Please, watch and enjoy!

00:48:43.950 --> 00:48:48.500
I swear to seize my happy ending at this School Festival!

00:48:48.500 --> 00:48:50.920
I must say, not having changed underwear for so long,

00:48:50.920 --> 00:48:53.450
I'm surprised you're even still alive...

00:48:53.450 --> 00:48:55.450
I did immediately fall sick.

00:48:55.450 --> 00:48:57.250
But I'm still kicking!

00:48:57.250 --> 00:48:58.870
It's the Speedy Kotatsu!

00:48:58.870 --> 00:49:00.220
Hold it right there!

00:49:00.600 --> 00:49:01.640
Time to go.

00:49:03.560 --> 00:49:06.010
Hey ho!

00:49:06.010 --> 00:49:07.530
Stop!

00:49:11.200 --> 00:49:12.510
Over here!

00:49:18.930 --> 00:49:21.140
The Princess isn't coming! She's been caught!

00:49:21.140 --> 00:49:22.080
Again?!

00:49:22.080 --> 00:49:23.470
We're out of understudies!

00:49:23.470 --> 00:49:24.550
You do it, then.

00:49:24.550 --> 00:49:25.230
Heck no!

00:49:25.230 --> 00:49:26.090
Hey, you.

00:49:26.090 --> 00:49:27.180
You wanna be an actress?

00:49:27.180 --> 00:49:28.380
Whatever, you're doing it.

00:49:28.380 --> 00:49:29.490
Here's your script!

00:49:32.820 --> 00:49:34.910
We can feed you your lines, too.

00:49:36.590 --> 00:49:38.440
Unnecessary! I've memorized it all.

00:49:40.070 --> 00:49:42.290
I shan't tuck my tail between my legs and run!

00:49:42.290 --> 00:49:45.070
It must be fate that I've been handed such a major role!

00:49:45.070 --> 00:49:47.460
I've resolved to follow my thread of fate until the end!

00:49:49.140 --> 00:49:53.080
You caught your cold from that Obscene Investigation Team, did you not?

00:49:53.080 --> 00:49:54.890
It's not the Obscene Investigation Team!

00:49:54.890 --> 00:49:56.650
It's the Bedchamber Investigation Team!

00:49:56.650 --> 00:49:58.980
By bedchamber, you mean a lady's bedroom!

00:49:58.980 --> 00:50:01.680
Investigation there is done only by the indecent and shameless!

00:50:01.680 --> 00:50:04.010
The name Depraved Director suits you well!

00:50:05.500 --> 00:50:10.080
That reprehensible sickness you bear

00:50:10.080 --> 00:50:14.760
To such baseness, I shall never yield

00:50:15.300 --> 00:50:17.140
Until the day

00:50:17.140 --> 00:50:19.680
I lay eyes on you again

00:50:19.680 --> 00:50:22.260
My beloved Crackpot of Monte Cristo

00:50:22.260 --> 00:50:24.520
That Crackpot of Monte Cristo of yours

00:50:24.520 --> 00:50:28.130
Imprisonment was his fate

00:50:28.130 --> 00:50:30.420
Never again to return

00:50:30.420 --> 00:50:32.700
Neither his name nor his ideals

00:50:32.700 --> 00:50:35.550
Even if the path I follow

00:50:35.550 --> 00:50:39.270
Should lead me straight to the depths of hell

00:50:39.270 --> 00:50:44.680
Never shall I become plagued by doubt or fear

00:50:44.680 --> 00:50:48.150
Ever onward, I'll press forward

00:50:48.900 --> 00:50:52.540
If it's for the sake of the Crackpot of Monte Cristo!

00:50:53.800 --> 00:50:55.300
The Crackpot of Monte Cristo Players!

00:50:55.300 --> 00:50:56.920
Performing a play here violates the rules!

00:50:56.920 --> 00:50:57.380
Take it down, guys!
Performing a play here violates the rules!

00:50:57.380 --> 00:50:59.040
Surrender yourselves quietly!
Take it down, guys!

00:50:59.040 --> 00:50:59.390
Surrender yourselves quietly!

00:50:59.910 --> 00:51:01.800
Let the show go on, you pain in the ass!

00:51:01.800 --> 00:51:03.910
Don't give me your cold, Depraved Director!

00:51:03.910 --> 00:51:05.380
Stop this!

00:51:05.380 --> 00:51:06.420
Out of my way!

00:51:06.420 --> 00:51:07.920
Again?!

00:51:10.170 --> 00:51:12.670
Why are you always center stage?!

00:51:12.670 --> 00:51:15.160
They escaped our clutches once again!

00:51:15.160 --> 00:51:17.470
They have an 11th leading lady!

00:51:17.470 --> 00:51:20.680
Go ahead and keep catching us!
We have infinite understudies!

00:51:20.990 --> 00:51:24.320
So you say, but the latest one is lacking in acting ability.

00:51:24.320 --> 00:51:26.260
I'd wager you're running out.

00:51:27.320 --> 00:51:28.320
But isn't it odd?

00:51:28.320 --> 00:51:30.330
The script seems freshly written,

00:51:30.330 --> 00:51:32.350
but we have yet to find the author!

00:51:33.560 --> 00:51:36.760
If we capture the author, continuing the play will be impossible.

00:51:36.760 --> 00:51:37.830
Where could he be?

00:51:38.450 --> 00:51:39.520
Director!

00:51:39.970 --> 00:51:41.060
Hey, Director!

00:51:42.660 --> 00:51:44.690
We've just intercepted a text message!

00:51:44.690 --> 00:51:45.620
That's private!
We've just intercepted a text message!

00:51:45.620 --> 00:51:46.780
It's the latest script!
That's private!

00:51:46.780 --> 00:51:48.780
We've confiscated their new lyrics!

00:51:49.600 --> 00:51:52.010
Also, this poster was amongst the data!

00:51:52.010 --> 00:51:52.960
My God...

00:51:52.960 --> 00:51:54.600
The final scene is up next!

00:51:54.600 --> 00:51:56.470
A love scene grand finale?

00:51:56.470 --> 00:51:58.500
L-L-Love scene?!

00:51:58.500 --> 00:51:59.920
But where?!

00:51:59.920 --> 00:52:02.470
Take a look at this security footage!

00:52:03.180 --> 00:52:04.670
The Speedy Kotatsu...

00:52:10.810 --> 00:52:11.930
Wait, what's that?

00:52:12.980 --> 00:52:14.060
A daruma?

00:52:14.060 --> 00:52:16.160
Forgotten by the Speedy Kotatsu?

00:52:16.160 --> 00:52:17.670
If we rewind...

00:52:21.490 --> 00:52:23.460
So that's what's going on!

00:52:23.460 --> 00:52:24.980
How could I not have noticed?

00:52:24.980 --> 00:52:27.000
You! Bring up the Crackpot of Monte Cristo map!

00:52:27.980 --> 00:52:30.260
Now overlay the Speedy Kotatsu map!

00:52:31.610 --> 00:52:33.360
It's a perfect match!

00:52:33.360 --> 00:52:37.070
So the ringleaders of "The Crackpot of Monte Cristo" write the script at the kotatsu,

00:52:37.070 --> 00:52:40.450
and once they move, the troupe performs at their old location!

00:52:41.010 --> 00:52:42.140
Shit...

00:52:42.140 --> 00:52:45.020
The Speedy Kotatsu is on the move through the courtyard!

00:52:47.020 --> 00:52:49.020
It's Higuchi and Don Underwear!

00:52:49.020 --> 00:52:50.010
The Don?

00:52:50.010 --> 00:52:51.530
Depraved Director!

00:52:52.520 --> 00:52:55.210
Everyone everywhere is running roughshod...

00:52:55.210 --> 00:52:56.570
Catch that kotatsu!

00:52:56.570 --> 00:52:59.240
Keep Don Underwear from taking the stage at all costs!

00:53:04.760 --> 00:53:05.850
What's up next?

00:53:05.850 --> 00:53:09.740
Well, there's a love scene up next between you and Don Underwear.

00:53:09.740 --> 00:53:10.840
You fine with that?

00:53:10.840 --> 00:53:12.190
I may have no experience,

00:53:12.190 --> 00:53:15.630
but I'm ready and willing to answer drama's call!

00:53:15.630 --> 00:53:19.830
Underwear-senpai put on this play to search for an unrequited love.

00:53:19.830 --> 00:53:21.780
If this play becomes a hot topic on campus,

00:53:21.780 --> 00:53:24.200
his Apple Girl will definitely come watch!

00:53:24.200 --> 00:53:27.390
Underwear-senpai will lay his feelings bare once she appears!

00:53:27.390 --> 00:53:31.490
The fact that the Count and the Princess can't meet
is a metaphor for what he's going through!

00:53:31.490 --> 00:53:34.980
There's no way she won't respond to the Don's feelings of love!

00:53:34.980 --> 00:53:36.390
Then that seals it!

00:53:36.390 --> 00:53:39.470
Until our Apple Girl appears, the show must go on!

00:53:41.690 --> 00:53:43.790
Our connection to the Kotatsu's been discovered!

00:53:43.790 --> 00:53:46.340
They'll most likely be expecting us on the roof!

00:53:46.340 --> 00:53:48.200
Execute Plan O!

00:53:51.710 --> 00:53:52.710
Here we go!

00:53:55.230 --> 00:53:57.020
If the troupe isn't stopped,

00:53:57.020 --> 00:54:00.220
she'll have a love scene in public with Don Underwear...

00:54:00.220 --> 00:54:01.460
This is bad!

00:54:01.460 --> 00:54:04.010
This is most definitely not the script written in my heart!

00:54:04.820 --> 00:54:07.540
But if I can just make it to the stage,

00:54:07.540 --> 00:54:09.100
I can trade places with the Don!

00:54:09.910 --> 00:54:11.530
The two of us finally being united

00:54:11.530 --> 00:54:13.230
would be drama of the highest order!

00:54:14.060 --> 00:54:15.990
Director! We've located the Kotatsu!

00:54:17.760 --> 00:54:19.920
My Romantic Engine doesn't have enough horsepower!

00:54:19.920 --> 00:54:22.200
If I don't do something, the last act won't happen at all!

00:54:23.130 --> 00:54:24.540
Naoko-san!

00:54:29.160 --> 00:54:30.540
Oh, lord.

00:54:32.540 --> 00:54:34.770
<i>Romantic Engine, Activate Pure Love Nitro!</i>

00:54:34.770 --> 00:54:36.760
<i>If she's tonight's leading lady,</i>

00:54:36.760 --> 00:54:38.800
<i>then damn straight I'm going to be the leading man!</i>

00:54:41.800 --> 00:54:43.840
Hey, your belt's all twisted!

00:54:44.930 --> 00:54:46.420
Let me fix that for you.

00:54:49.140 --> 00:54:51.640
The only thing twisted here is my love-struck heart!

00:54:51.640 --> 00:54:52.750
What are you doing?!

00:54:52.750 --> 00:54:54.140
This isn't what you promised!

00:54:54.140 --> 00:54:56.400
The girl takes priority over everything else!

00:54:56.400 --> 00:54:58.650
That promise is about fifth on my list!

00:55:12.010 --> 00:55:13.870
Where's the Crackpot of Monte Cristo?!

00:55:14.520 --> 00:55:17.730
You've showed quite the hustle,
but this isn't the finish line.

00:55:17.730 --> 00:55:19.550
The final scene is taking place over there.

00:55:25.740 --> 00:55:27.780
The Crackpot of Monte Cristo! Begin!

00:55:32.040 --> 00:55:35.820
The Crackpot of Monte Cristo

00:55:35.820 --> 00:55:40.530
Has vanished, nowhere to be found

00:55:40.530 --> 00:55:42.780
And ever since

00:55:42.780 --> 00:55:46.820
The world has been as under lock and key to me

00:55:46.820 --> 00:55:49.410
Yet this time for sure

00:55:49.410 --> 00:55:54.910
My journey is almost at its end!

00:55:54.910 --> 00:55:59.920
This time, for sure!

00:56:06.930 --> 00:56:09.350
One day, on a bench

00:56:10.090 --> 00:56:11.930
I had taken my seat

00:56:11.930 --> 00:56:15.850
And you sat down nearby in turn

00:56:15.850 --> 00:56:18.530
And then, from up above

00:56:19.360 --> 00:56:21.200
A rain of apples

00:56:21.200 --> 00:56:23.600
And at the moment I saw you

00:56:23.600 --> 00:56:25.990
You looked my way as well!

00:56:25.990 --> 00:56:28.170
And then, on both our heads

00:56:28.170 --> 00:56:30.950
Out of nowhere, a thump!

00:56:31.580 --> 00:56:32.950
Two apples

00:56:32.950 --> 00:56:34.950
Out of nowhere, a thump.

00:56:34.950 --> 00:56:37.720
Such a twist of fate

00:56:38.290 --> 00:56:39.890
This divine revelation

00:56:39.890 --> 00:56:41.470
At that moment, I knew it was love!

00:56:41.470 --> 00:56:43.670
Th-That's...
At that moment, I knew it was love!

00:56:43.990 --> 00:56:46.070
I adore you

00:56:46.070 --> 00:56:49.210
My destined love

00:56:49.210 --> 00:56:51.140
Princess...

00:56:51.140 --> 00:56:52.960
This is a festival of fools.
Daruma!

00:56:52.960 --> 00:56:54.450
Keep watching, and you'll become one, too.
Daruma!

00:56:54.450 --> 00:56:55.410
Keep watching, and you'll become one, too.

00:56:55.410 --> 00:56:57.090
If I'm going to be a fool anyway,

00:56:57.640 --> 00:56:58.640
Then I'll

00:56:59.460 --> 00:57:02.150
be a <i>dancing</i> fool!

00:57:07.650 --> 00:57:09.440
Something's caught on the net!

00:57:09.440 --> 00:57:10.290
Raise it up!

00:57:29.630 --> 00:57:30.630
Music!

00:57:35.590 --> 00:57:39.210
I happened to be passing through by chance

00:57:39.210 --> 00:57:41.990
But to be able to meet you like this

00:57:41.990 --> 00:57:44.290
Is such a marvelous joy

00:57:44.290 --> 00:57:45.440
Who's this idiot?!
Is such a marvelous joy

00:57:45.440 --> 00:57:45.590
I'm just a poor seller of Ra Ta Ta Tam
Who's this idiot?!

00:57:45.590 --> 00:57:47.530
I'm just a poor seller of Ra Ta Ta Tam

00:57:47.530 --> 00:57:48.370
Get lost!
I'm just a poor seller of Ra Ta Ta Tam

00:57:48.370 --> 00:57:48.840
And so, my raven-haired maiden
Get lost!

00:57:48.840 --> 00:57:50.780
And so, my raven-haired maiden

00:57:51.430 --> 00:57:53.710
It is I, the Senpai you often meet

00:57:53.710 --> 00:57:55.190
What's this crap?!
It is I, the Senpai you often meet

00:57:55.190 --> 00:57:55.810
The hell?!
It is I, the Senpai you often meet

00:57:55.810 --> 00:57:56.370
Senpai, such a coincidence
The hell?!

00:57:56.370 --> 00:57:58.530
Senpai, such a coincidence

00:57:58.530 --> 00:58:00.460
No, simply by chance!

00:58:00.460 --> 00:58:02.090
Such a coincidence

00:58:02.090 --> 00:58:03.150
No, just by chance!

00:58:03.150 --> 00:58:04.020
A coincidence

00:58:04.020 --> 00:58:04.970
By chance!

00:58:04.970 --> 00:58:05.500
Coinci—

00:58:05.500 --> 00:58:05.900
Chance!

00:58:05.900 --> 00:58:06.350
Coin—

00:58:06.350 --> 00:58:06.810
Chance!

00:58:06.810 --> 00:58:07.150
Co...

00:58:07.150 --> 00:58:07.590
...ance!

00:58:07.590 --> 00:58:12.590
I suppose, then, it must be fate!

00:58:13.590 --> 00:58:15.220
<i>Well, time for the kiss.</i>

00:58:15.220 --> 00:58:16.760
<i>But this isn't how she really feels...</i>

00:58:16.760 --> 00:58:19.100
<i>It's a play! An act of dramatic necessity!</i>

00:58:20.600 --> 00:58:21.540
Senpai?

00:58:23.630 --> 00:58:26.610
I am the one, the leading man

00:58:26.610 --> 00:58:29.010
This play's grand conspirator

00:58:29.010 --> 00:58:31.740
A disruption, quite unexpected

00:58:31.740 --> 00:58:34.200
Just jammed up the works

00:58:34.200 --> 00:58:36.990
But please, forget about that now

00:58:36.990 --> 00:58:39.430
Keep your eyes focused on me!

00:58:39.430 --> 00:58:44.750
Ah! My darling, lovely Apple Girl!

00:58:44.750 --> 00:58:47.330
If you're out there, out there somewhere

00:58:47.330 --> 00:58:50.690
Then please, won't you now take the stage?

00:58:50.690 --> 00:58:51.960
I suppose you mean me?
Then please, won't you now take the stage?

00:59:02.410 --> 00:59:05.520
Isn't it strange, a coincidence

00:59:05.520 --> 00:59:08.410
A bolt from the blue

00:59:08.410 --> 00:59:11.630
That once again, in this place

00:59:11.630 --> 00:59:14.470
I should lay my eyes on you

00:59:14.470 --> 00:59:17.610
Destiny layered in destiny

00:59:17.610 --> 00:59:20.450
How can it be that you and I

00:59:20.450 --> 00:59:23.640
Had been waiting, oh so long

00:59:23.640 --> 00:59:26.660
My person of destiny

00:59:26.660 --> 00:59:33.170
By heaven's decree, it's you, Don Underwear!

00:59:34.530 --> 00:59:36.870
A-Apple Girl...

00:59:36.870 --> 00:59:38.660
It's you!

00:59:39.440 --> 00:59:40.810
My deepest apologies.

00:59:40.810 --> 00:59:43.310
Consider yourself caught!

00:59:44.310 --> 00:59:45.220
Underwear!

00:59:45.220 --> 00:59:46.870
You public-moral-flouting scoundrel!

00:59:46.870 --> 00:59:48.810
It is I, the School Festival Executive Director!

00:59:49.520 --> 00:59:53.820
Your beloved Apple Girl was a mere disguise—
an idol I dress up as for my own amusement!

00:59:53.820 --> 00:59:55.700
I apologize for never telling you.

01:00:07.570 --> 01:00:09.380
Am I

01:00:10.120 --> 01:00:12.220
Just not good enough

01:00:13.010 --> 01:00:15.800
My dear Don Underwear

01:00:15.800 --> 01:00:19.010
You were always, always on my mind

01:00:19.010 --> 01:00:20.990
Always have I

01:00:20.990 --> 01:00:24.330
Been left staring at your back

01:00:24.330 --> 01:00:29.170
Supporting you this entire time

01:00:30.410 --> 01:00:32.980
However

01:00:32.980 --> 01:00:35.810
In your heart

01:00:35.810 --> 01:00:38.070
There lives someone different

01:00:38.630 --> 01:00:42.870
If all you desire is a woman of beauty

01:00:42.870 --> 01:00:45.570
Then what about cosmetic surgery?

01:00:45.570 --> 01:00:51.140
Even that, I would consider

01:00:51.140 --> 01:00:53.290
Won't you please just look my way?!

01:00:53.290 --> 01:00:55.270
Do it!

01:00:55.270 --> 01:00:56.970
Look her way!

01:00:57.240 --> 01:00:59.130
Get lost, Depraved Director!

01:00:59.130 --> 01:01:00.910
Get back to your Bedchamber!

01:01:03.480 --> 01:01:05.340
I'm sorry, but

01:01:05.340 --> 01:01:08.180
That's something I just can't do

01:01:08.180 --> 01:01:10.610
What I fell in love with

01:01:10.610 --> 01:01:15.080
Was not a face, but the thump of an apple

01:01:15.080 --> 01:01:17.790
It was at that moment

01:01:17.790 --> 01:01:22.180
I knew that my fate had been sealed

01:01:22.860 --> 01:01:25.030
Even if

01:01:25.030 --> 01:01:27.120
My beloved

01:01:27.120 --> 01:01:29.540
Should happen to be a man

01:01:29.540 --> 01:01:35.710
The pounding of my heart can tell no lies

01:01:37.710 --> 01:01:40.470
You idiot romanticism fundamentalist!

01:01:40.470 --> 01:01:42.220
Look at the girl standing in front of you!

01:01:58.610 --> 01:02:01.950
Such determined words do not go unheard

01:02:01.950 --> 01:02:05.170
I long for nothing more than someone to cure my loneliness

01:02:05.170 --> 01:02:08.780
Yet I am the one in charge, the Festival Director

01:02:08.780 --> 01:02:13.420
There is no one who can understand my troubles

01:02:15.490 --> 01:02:18.770
Yet if you were willing to take me in your arms

01:02:18.770 --> 01:02:24.090
Then in that case, for you, a woman I can be!

01:02:26.470 --> 01:02:28.970
Is your fever getting to you?!
You're taking opportunism too far!

01:02:44.070 --> 01:02:45.820
<i>Just give me the cue!</i>

01:02:45.820 --> 01:02:47.080
<i>Just play the music!</i>

01:02:47.080 --> 01:02:49.070
No! Don't signal it!

01:02:49.070 --> 01:02:51.580
Seeking another's warmth just to cure transitory loneliness?

01:02:51.580 --> 01:02:53.080
Utterly preposterous!

01:03:03.590 --> 01:03:05.620
Yuko! Jirokichi!

01:03:05.620 --> 01:03:07.830
My koi!

01:03:15.360 --> 01:03:16.840
These koi

01:03:16.840 --> 01:03:19.470
Have birthed a new love

01:03:19.470 --> 01:03:23.830
This time for sure, a destined love

01:03:23.830 --> 01:03:28.090
Love, ever fickle

01:03:28.090 --> 01:03:31.960
Love, ever selfish

01:03:32.440 --> 01:03:36.710
But at the end I've finally met you

01:03:36.710 --> 01:03:41.190
My one and true destiny

01:03:43.040 --> 01:03:47.410
The story, as always, is opportunism

01:03:47.410 --> 01:03:51.870
Finally, you looked my way

01:03:51.870 --> 01:03:52.110
I know that you

01:03:52.110 --> 01:03:53.370
They're alive...
I know that you

01:03:53.370 --> 01:03:54.930
I know they're alive...!
I know that you

01:03:54.930 --> 01:03:55.860
I know that you

01:03:55.860 --> 01:04:00.040
You are my destined love

01:04:00.680 --> 01:04:12.400
In our rose-colored campus life!

01:04:22.220 --> 01:04:24.670
<i>Before I'd realized it, I had caught a cold.</i>

01:04:28.530 --> 01:04:32.390
<i>I muttered out my symptoms on social media but got no response.</i>

01:04:32.390 --> 01:04:33.660
<i>Was everyone still out?</i>

01:04:33.660 --> 01:04:36.390
<i>Or perhaps the thought of associating with me was too unbearable.</i>

01:04:36.990 --> 01:04:40.360
<i>An evening that seemed to encompass every season had left me beat...</i>

01:04:40.360 --> 01:04:42.980
<i>I doubt I'll be putting away my bed for some time.</i>

01:04:55.270 --> 01:04:57.560
<i>Then what of me, all alone...</i>

01:04:57.560 --> 01:04:59.930
<i>Then what of me, all alone?!</i>

01:05:03.000 --> 01:05:06.350
If you're making egg saké,
leave out the egg and the sugar.

01:05:06.350 --> 01:05:07.570
Not going to happen.

01:05:07.570 --> 01:05:10.340
You're sick because you allowed your spirit to falter.

01:05:10.340 --> 01:05:11.870
You should follow my example.

01:05:11.870 --> 01:05:15.230
<i>You</i> didn't catch a cold because you're an idiot.

01:05:15.230 --> 01:05:18.680
Although I'll admit I'm happy you dropped by to see me...

01:05:18.680 --> 01:05:22.640
My main source of food becoming laid up in bed leaves me in danger of starvation, after all.

01:05:22.640 --> 01:05:24.600
Not that I could have done anything to help.

01:05:24.600 --> 01:05:26.530
Thank goodness she's here too.

01:05:27.600 --> 01:05:29.580
This is a lot tastier than I expected!

01:05:29.580 --> 01:05:30.660
So, how is everyone else?

01:05:30.660 --> 01:05:33.550
It seems like the entire city is fighting off a cold.

01:05:33.550 --> 01:05:36.700
If you go outside, it's almost like a ghost town.

01:05:36.700 --> 01:05:38.910
You must be tough if you haven't caught it yet!

01:05:38.910 --> 01:05:42.920
If we had some Junpero, this epidemic would be over in an instant.

01:05:43.370 --> 01:05:47.590
The legendary wonder drug used in the treatment of tuberculosis ages ago...

01:05:47.590 --> 01:05:51.330
When it's swirled on a stick like candy, one lick can lower any fever.

01:05:51.330 --> 01:05:53.930
One's body is filled to the brim with vitality once more.

01:05:54.690 --> 01:05:57.170
That's right! Rihaku-san would have some for sure!

01:05:57.170 --> 01:05:59.360
I sense another profitable venture ahead...

01:06:09.140 --> 01:06:10.450
Don Underwear!

01:06:12.390 --> 01:06:14.360
Oh... Hey...

01:06:14.360 --> 01:06:16.260
I'm wearing new underwear...

01:06:16.260 --> 01:06:17.790
S-So I'm...

01:06:17.790 --> 01:06:19.520
Are you all right?!

01:06:19.520 --> 01:06:21.610
Noriko-kun's cold...

01:06:21.610 --> 01:06:23.570
It's an awful beast...

01:06:23.570 --> 01:06:25.130
I'm off to shee her...

01:06:25.720 --> 01:06:27.270
You'll both end up in trouble!

01:06:27.270 --> 01:06:28.800
I'll go with you!

01:06:29.510 --> 01:06:31.300
There's nothing better if you're sick!

01:06:31.680 --> 01:06:35.040
Cola has secret ingredients inside,

01:06:35.040 --> 01:06:36.820
and they work well on colds.

01:06:36.820 --> 01:06:39.220
If you add some ginger, too...

01:06:40.160 --> 01:06:42.320
...the effect is increased a hundredfold.

01:06:55.100 --> 01:06:56.070
Delicious.

01:06:56.070 --> 01:06:58.620
It's my mother's secret egg saké recipe.

01:06:59.290 --> 01:07:01.420
I'd rather not look like I'm upstaging the Don,

01:07:01.420 --> 01:07:03.580
so keep this our little secret.

01:07:03.580 --> 01:07:05.100
Thanks for going out of your way.

01:07:05.960 --> 01:07:08.660
But you need to dress warmer or you'll get sick, too!

01:07:08.660 --> 01:07:09.900
Want one of my sweaters?

01:07:09.900 --> 01:07:10.800
I'll be fine!

01:07:10.800 --> 01:07:11.830
No, you won't.

01:07:12.590 --> 01:07:15.590
Those round cushions are really cute.

01:07:15.590 --> 01:07:17.910
I bought <i>way</i> too many of them.

01:07:17.910 --> 01:07:19.940
But squeezing them feels so nice,

01:07:19.940 --> 01:07:21.600
and they're fun, too.

01:07:21.990 --> 01:07:25.020
You know, it's a waste if I'm the only one having your egg saké.

01:07:25.020 --> 01:07:27.110
Could you bring some to the Director?

01:07:27.110 --> 01:07:29.960
He's all by himself, so he's probably feeling down.

01:07:29.960 --> 01:07:31.110
Certainly!

01:07:31.540 --> 01:07:34.600
And bring some Ginger Cola with you, too...

01:07:37.070 --> 01:07:39.080
Apologies for making you go out of your way.

01:07:39.450 --> 01:07:42.450
As you can see, my popularity is burying me alive.

01:07:42.450 --> 01:07:45.340
So many people sent you gifts!

01:07:45.340 --> 01:07:49.670
My performance in that musical brought me a lot of new fans from across campus.

01:07:49.670 --> 01:07:52.030
So please, don't concern yourself with me.

01:07:52.030 --> 01:07:56.250
However, since I seem to have given my cold to most of my guests,

01:07:56.250 --> 01:07:58.020
it does pain my heart somewhat.

01:07:58.020 --> 01:07:59.440
The one I'm most worried about

01:07:59.440 --> 01:08:02.890
is my colleague from the Bedchamber Investigation Team, Toudou-san.

01:08:02.890 --> 01:08:04.710
His daughter has yet to visit him,

01:08:04.710 --> 01:08:07.900
and he must be lonely wrapped up in bed by himself.

01:08:07.900 --> 01:08:08.900
I'll go visit him.

01:08:08.900 --> 01:08:10.070
Really?

01:08:10.070 --> 01:08:12.990
There are some apples over there,
so would you mind bringing some with?

01:08:12.990 --> 01:08:14.820
An apple a day and all that...

01:08:14.820 --> 01:08:15.470
Of course!

01:08:15.470 --> 01:08:19.320
A tornado ruined the crop last year,
but this time it's been quite the harvest.

01:08:19.690 --> 01:08:22.330
I also received a bunch of hats, so please, help yourself.

01:08:22.850 --> 01:08:25.360
Your ears do look quite cold.

01:08:27.020 --> 01:08:29.330
So, what happened afterwards?

01:08:29.330 --> 01:08:33.460
With the senpai you keep bumping into
who tried to take over the Crackpot of Monte Cristo.

01:08:33.460 --> 01:08:36.340
That was... He was just passing through by chance.

01:08:36.340 --> 01:08:39.700
Really now! He practically hijacked the play.

01:08:39.700 --> 01:08:41.450
He is my friend, after all,

01:08:41.450 --> 01:08:43.850
and that was the first time I'd ever seen him so frantic.

01:08:44.370 --> 01:08:46.330
But I suppose you wouldn't understand.

01:08:46.330 --> 01:08:50.050
You push forward so relentlessly that no one can catch up to you.

01:08:50.050 --> 01:08:52.150
And yet he always just happens to be passing through.

01:08:52.150 --> 01:08:53.860
Haven't you found it strange?

01:08:54.370 --> 01:08:57.320
<i>Up to this point, I've been complete absorbed in funteresting things,</i>

01:08:57.320 --> 01:08:59.430
<i>walking the road wherever it led.</i>

01:08:59.430 --> 01:09:03.370
<i>I've been especially lax in learning the tactics required for romantic relationships.</i>

01:09:03.370 --> 01:09:05.870
<i>And never mind noticing the feelings of others—</i>

01:09:05.870 --> 01:09:10.880
<i>just trying to grasp my own feelings, vague and fluffy like cotton candy, is no mean feat.</i>

01:09:10.880 --> 01:09:15.260
<i>But when I remember Senpai wrapping his arms around my papier mache costume,</i>

01:09:15.260 --> 01:09:19.380
<i>something inside of me goes "Pop!" and makes me want to hug my red carp.</i>

01:09:21.390 --> 01:09:23.390
Yahoo!

01:09:23.390 --> 01:09:26.450
<i>Did that really happen?</i>

01:09:26.450 --> 01:09:29.390
<i>It wasn't all just my imagination, was it?</i>

01:09:29.390 --> 01:09:31.400
Yahoo...

01:09:39.560 --> 01:09:42.660
What dragged you all the way out here?

01:09:42.660 --> 01:09:45.910
The Festival Director told me where you live.

01:09:45.910 --> 01:09:47.610
I thought he was pissed at me...

01:09:47.610 --> 01:09:49.480
I did give him this cold, after all.

01:09:49.480 --> 01:09:52.380
I think he was more worried about you than himself.

01:09:52.380 --> 01:09:56.350
My daughter did come to visit,
but she ended up gettin' my cold...

01:09:56.350 --> 01:09:59.240
And apparently passed it on to her husband and her new in-laws too.

01:09:59.240 --> 01:10:01.570
Heck, you might end up gettin' it too.

01:10:01.570 --> 01:10:03.920
It seems the God of Colds and I are on the outs.

01:10:03.920 --> 01:10:05.210
For pete's sake...

01:10:05.210 --> 01:10:07.560
Here you are lookin' out for me again.

01:10:08.570 --> 01:10:13.130
Hey, I met some kid searchin' for some old book at the market. I think he said he was your senpai?

01:10:13.130 --> 01:10:15.410
He wanted some lousy kid's book called Ra Ta Ta Tam.

01:10:15.410 --> 01:10:18.850
Seems he wanted to get his hands on it at any cost.

01:10:18.850 --> 01:10:22.100
I practically begged him to get me that piece of erotic art instead, but...

01:10:22.100 --> 01:10:25.660
Whatever, I ended up gettin' my hands on it anyway.

01:10:25.660 --> 01:10:29.160
Not for free, though. I picked up this cold from Rihaku-san.

01:10:29.160 --> 01:10:32.520
He already had it back at your drinking contest,

01:10:32.520 --> 01:10:35.170
and it sounds like it's only gotten worse since then.

01:10:43.580 --> 01:10:44.180
Oh!

01:10:44.180 --> 01:10:46.680
Why are the streets so deserted today?

01:10:46.680 --> 01:10:49.680
This cold lays in ambush attacking anyone who approaches.

01:10:49.680 --> 01:10:53.440
I thought the apocalypse happened while I was wrapped up in bed.

01:10:54.590 --> 01:10:56.080
Oh, you won't believe this!

01:10:56.080 --> 01:10:58.190
Higuchi-kun finally got sick, too!

01:11:02.110 --> 01:11:06.560
I had planned on visiting Rihaku-san, but the closer I got, the more merciless the wind became.

01:11:06.560 --> 01:11:09.810
Alas, my attempt at the journey ended in tragic defeat.

01:11:09.810 --> 01:11:11.530
This is no mere common cold.

01:11:11.530 --> 01:11:15.210
This retrovirus gone rampant is none other than the Rihaku Cold!

01:11:15.210 --> 01:11:17.710
May I ask you where Rihaku-san lives?

01:11:17.710 --> 01:11:20.960
He parks his train in an isolated area by Takaragaike Lake,

01:11:20.960 --> 01:11:23.160
where winds are constantly gushing out.

01:11:23.160 --> 01:11:25.960
The God of Colds inside of Rihaku sends forth its minions,

01:11:25.960 --> 01:11:28.580
and the wind sends them swirling through Kyoto!

01:11:28.580 --> 01:11:32.230
If we do nothing, double suicide between Kyoto and Rihaku-san will be the inevitable end!

01:11:32.880 --> 01:11:35.730
I'm on my way to go visit Rihaku-san now!

01:11:36.100 --> 01:11:38.230
Look what happened to Higuchi-kun when he tried!

01:11:38.230 --> 01:11:43.730
I had thought that the God of Colds wants nothing to do with me, but it seems this must be fate.

01:11:43.730 --> 01:11:46.740
There's something I must tell Rihaku-san in person!

01:12:07.070 --> 01:12:09.530
Apologies for dropping in so late!

01:12:09.530 --> 01:12:12.890
Rihaku-san! Rihaku-san!

01:12:14.800 --> 01:12:15.770
Rihaku-san!

01:12:15.770 --> 01:12:18.850
I'm on my deathbed...

01:12:18.850 --> 01:12:21.110
You mustn't give in so easily!

01:12:22.120 --> 01:12:24.340
It seems you haven't changed...

01:12:24.940 --> 01:12:28.520
How many decades have passed since our drinking contest?

01:12:32.120 --> 01:12:33.700
It hasn't been that long.

01:12:33.700 --> 01:12:35.750
It was only a few hours ago, this very night!

01:12:35.750 --> 01:12:37.930
If only that were so.

01:12:37.930 --> 01:12:43.070
Time in isolation flies like an arrow, and now years and decades have gone by....

01:12:44.580 --> 01:12:49.210
On such a lonely winter's night, I'm weeping like an infant with a soiled diaper.

01:12:49.210 --> 01:12:52.050
No matter how much I wail,
my mother doesn't appear...

01:12:52.050 --> 01:12:53.810
But I'm here now.

01:12:53.810 --> 01:12:57.840
I used to love collecting and trading valuable milk caps at exorbitant rates.

01:12:57.840 --> 01:13:00.960
In Sevens, I loved ensuring play couldn't continue past 6 or 8,

01:13:00.960 --> 01:13:03.860
and I happily drunk in everyone's troubled faces.

01:13:04.210 --> 01:13:08.080
My parents didn't come home very often, but I had money,

01:13:08.080 --> 01:13:10.560
and with money came friends.

01:13:10.560 --> 01:13:11.870
As did women.

01:13:12.450 --> 01:13:13.500
However...

01:13:13.500 --> 01:13:16.450
There were those who stole what I had through brute force,

01:13:16.450 --> 01:13:18.400
and in the end I had nothing.

01:13:18.400 --> 01:13:22.080
I knew then the world was a scramble, full of nothing but taking...

01:13:22.080 --> 01:13:24.270
But strength, too, can be bought with money.

01:13:24.270 --> 01:13:25.710
So can love.

01:13:25.710 --> 01:13:28.380
There is nothing on earth that money can't buy.

01:13:28.380 --> 01:13:29.130
Yet...

01:13:29.130 --> 01:13:32.300
No matter how much I collected, my heart remained unfulfilled.

01:13:32.300 --> 01:13:34.680
Rihaku-san, you're not alone.

01:13:34.680 --> 01:13:36.810
You're connected to others,
whatever you might think!

01:13:37.330 --> 01:13:40.050
The money you loaned out to people became their strength,

01:13:40.050 --> 01:13:43.360
and after having its fun,
it returned to you once again.

01:13:43.670 --> 01:13:46.220
Your cold was first transferred to Hanuki-san,

01:13:46.220 --> 01:13:48.040
then to Toudou-san and the Director,

01:13:48.040 --> 01:13:50.440
the Don, Noriko-san, and all their friends,

01:13:50.440 --> 01:13:52.570
and then to friends of those friends.

01:13:52.570 --> 01:13:54.740
It's spreading all throughout the city!

01:13:54.740 --> 01:13:59.710
And the things you stole bounced from one place to the next, bringing happiness with them.

01:14:04.090 --> 01:14:06.060
Even as you profess your isolation,

01:14:06.060 --> 01:14:08.410
you're still bound to others in the end.

01:14:08.410 --> 01:14:12.760
Everyone is connected to the threads of fate you weave, whether they like it or not.

01:14:13.100 --> 01:14:16.170
Rihaku-san, you're absolutely not alone!

01:14:16.170 --> 01:14:18.880
You've given me an irreplaceable evening—

01:14:18.880 --> 01:14:21.270
a long and marvelous night!

01:14:26.690 --> 01:14:28.300
Thank you.

01:14:38.060 --> 01:14:42.330
I had such a wonderful evening thanks to you, Rihaku-san.

01:14:42.330 --> 01:14:44.790
The Fake Denki Brandy was quite delicious.

01:14:44.790 --> 01:14:47.800
Shall we have some more, then?

01:14:48.590 --> 01:14:50.740
I'll drink until there's nothing left.

01:14:54.340 --> 01:14:55.800
What's that?

01:14:55.800 --> 01:15:00.070
It appears there's a virus out there even worse than what I had.

01:15:00.070 --> 01:15:02.280
A terminal case if I ever saw one.

01:15:02.280 --> 01:15:06.960
A young man is struggling with isolation to a greater degree than I did.

01:15:06.960 --> 01:15:09.320
Would you perhaps have an idea who it could be?

01:15:09.660 --> 01:15:12.130
Now that I think of it, someone does come to mind...

01:15:12.130 --> 01:15:14.880
Do you remember the story of Ra Ta Ta Tam?

01:15:14.880 --> 01:15:17.900
That small white train had a destination in mind...

01:15:17.900 --> 01:15:21.780
Just as you have a final station to reach as well.

01:15:21.780 --> 01:15:22.580
Yes!

01:15:22.580 --> 01:15:24.820
The dawn is drawing near...

01:15:24.820 --> 01:15:26.830
The night is short!

01:15:26.830 --> 01:15:29.130
Walk on, young maiden!

01:15:31.880 --> 01:15:35.620
A cure for the cold that no regular medicine will cure!

01:15:35.620 --> 01:15:36.890
It's Junpero!

01:15:39.300 --> 01:15:46.130
Life is indeed short, my dear

01:15:46.130 --> 01:15:54.070
So, young lady, do fall in love

01:15:54.550 --> 01:15:56.410
